course: dictionary
lesson: 1792
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word clock is a good example. «Josh stares at the clock: "It's moved one minute in, like, an hour."» Here a clock is the machine on the wall that shows the time.
explain: Now look at «She clocked 12 seconds.» There is no machine here. To clock means to measure a time or a speed, so she was timed at 12 seconds. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try it in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Clock also appears in phrases. «Three o'clock» names an exact hour, and «around the clock» means all day and night. Phrases like these are best learned as a whole, not word by word.
fact: A clock is a machine that shows the time.
fact: «O'clock» names an exact hour, as in «three o'clock».
fact: To clock means to measure a time or a speed, as in «She clocked 12 seconds».
fact: On a clock face there are 12 hours; the short hand shows hours and the long hand shows minutes.
fact: «Around the clock» means all day and night, and «against the clock» means racing to finish before a time limit.
exercise: «Three o'clock» names what? | A speed | A kind of watch | *An exact hour | A wall
exercise: «She clocked 12 seconds.» What does clocked mean? | Ran away | *Measured the time | Cleaned the clock | Stopped the clock
exercise: On a clock face, what does the short hand show? | *Hours | Days | Minutes | Seconds
test: «From 7:30 am to 1:30 pm is 6 hours.» How many hours is that? | 7 | 8 | *6 | 5
test: «Going east, the clock usually moves one hour» what? | *Later | Not at all | Backwards | Earlier
exam: «Around the clock» means what? | Very fast | Only at noon | Once a week | *All day and night
